reply.body:
Your observation is correct, but I don't understand your comment "*we pass null to filter for all engines in the queue*"? From looking at the code of `getQueuedTargets()`, passing a `null` argument for the engine wouldn't return any compilation at all:
```java
        for (CompilationTask.ExecutorServiceWrapper wrapper : array) {
            OptimizedCallTarget target = wrapper.compileTask.targetRef.get();
            if (target != null && target.engine == engine) {
                queuedTargets.add(target);
            }
        }
```
Did I misunderstood you or do you propose that I change `getQueuedTargets()` to treat a `null` engine as a filter for "all engines"?

